{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-08-12T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A line of elephants emerges from the morning haze, calves keeping pace beside older relatives as they head towards a marsh. In Amboseli National Park, scenes like this unfold every day, shaped by water hidden beneath the ground. Meltwater from Mount Kilimanjaro filters through volcanic rock before surfacing as springs that keep the park's wetlands alive, even when the surrounding plains are dry. These permanent water sources sustain elephants, buffaloes, hippos and many other animals, while acacia woodland and open grassland support predators such as lions and cheetahs.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ElephantDay_ROW7064675180_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ElephantDay_ROW7064675180_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"A group of elephants, Amboseli National Park, Kenya","Copyright":"© Ibrahim Suha Derbent/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260812_ElephantDay\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Amboseli+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260812_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260812_ElephantDay"},"Ssd":"20260812","Name":"ElephantDay","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7064675180","FullDateString":"12 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Ships, storms and changing technology have come and gone, but the light remains. On Washington's San Juan Island, Lime Kiln Lighthouse has overlooked Haro Strait since 1919. Perched on a rocky bluff, its white flash continues to guide vessels through one of the Pacific Northwest's most important inland waterways. The lighthouse stands within Lime Kiln Point State Park, widely regarded as one of the world's best places to watch wild orcas from shore, with whales sometimes passing remarkably close to the coast.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LimeKiln_ROW6859587054_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LimeKiln_ROW6859587054_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Lime Kiln Lighthouse on San Juan Island, Washington state, United States","Copyright":"© Edmund Lowe Photography/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260811_LimeKiln\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lime+Kiln+Lighthouse&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260811_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260811_LimeKiln"},"Ssd":"20260811","Name":"LimeKiln","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6859587054","FullDateString":"11 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The best route here isn't built with concrete. Instead, the tide reveals a rocky path leading from Whytecliff Park to Whyte Islet in West Vancouver, Canada. A few hours later, the sea quietly covers the crossing again, making timing part of the experience. This shoreline has drawn visitors for generations. The tide opens the path; wet rocks keep you humble. The reward is a sweeping view back towards the beach and the hillside homes of Gleneagles.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.WhyteCliffP_ROW6700227959_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.WhyteCliffP_ROW6700227959_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Whytecliff Park, West Vancouver, Canada","Copyright":"© Aolin Chen/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260810_WhyteCliffP\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Whytecliff+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260810_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260810_WhyteCliffP"},"Ssd":"20260810","Name":"WhyteCliffP","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6700227959","FullDateString":"10 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"At first glance, they look like giant wooden shells rising above the trees. Look a little closer and every curve has a purpose. The Jean-Marie Tjibaou Cultural Centre, which opened in 1998, celebrates the Kanak people, the Indigenous inhabitants of New Caledonia, whose traditions, languages and customs have shaped the archipelago for thousands of years. Italian architect Renzo Piano designed the complex after studying traditional Kanak building techniques, reinterpreting them with laminated timber ribs, steel frames and modern engineering. Rather than copying historic structures, he created a contemporary design inspired by traditional Kanak grandes cases, or ceremonial houses.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.JMTjibaou_ROW6533820010_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.JMTjibaou_ROW6533820010_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Jean-Marie Tjibaou Cultural Centre, New Caledonia","Copyright":"© Fabien Astre/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260809_JMTjibaou\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Jean+Marie+Tjibaou+Cultural+Centre&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260809_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260809_JMTjibaou"},"Ssd":"20260809","Name":"JMTjibaou","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6533820010","FullDateString":"9 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Nature has a knack for balancing the impossible. In New Mexico's Ah-Shi-Sle-Pah Wilderness, towering hoodoos perch hefty rock caps on slender stems. Wind, water and ice have spent roughly 75 million years sculpting these remote badlands into an open-air gallery that feels more alien than terrestrial.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ValleyDreams_ROW6376883591_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ValleyDreams_ROW6376883591_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Hoodoos in Ah Shi Sle Pah Wilderness in San Juan County, New Mexico, United States","Copyright":"© Westend61/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260808_ValleyDreams\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Ah+Shi+Sle+Pah+Wilderness&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260808_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260808_ValleyDreams"},"Ssd":"20260808","Name":"ValleyDreams","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6376883591","FullDateString":"8 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In Copenhagen, Nyhavn Canal is a burst of colour and history. In Denmark's capital, bright, gabled houses lean toward the water, their reflections rippling beside old wooden ships. Carved out in the 1670s under King Christian V, this 17th-century canal once served as a busy gateway where cargo vessels unloaded goods straight into the city's heart. Sailors crowded its taverns, and the harbour gained a rough reputation long before it became the postcard-perfect place seen today.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ColorfulCop_ROW6097405388_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ColorfulCop_ROW6097405388_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Colourful homes line Nyhavn Canal, Copenhagen, Denmark","Copyright":"© emicristea/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260807_ColorfulCop\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Nyhavn+Canal+Copenhagen&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260807_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260807_ColorfulCop"},"Ssd":"20260807","Name":"ColorfulCop","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6097405388","FullDateString":"7 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In the Masai Mara, Kenya, the ground seems to move. A vast surge of wildebeest—hoofed grazers built for endurance—travel in tightly packed herds, drawn by fresh grass and water replenished by seasonal rains.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MaraCrossing_ROW6582779125_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MaraCrossing_ROW6582779125_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Migrating wildebeest crossing Mara River in Masai Mara, Kenya","Copyright":"© Manoj Shah/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260806_MaraCrossing\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Wildebeest&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260806_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260806_MaraCrossing"},"Ssd":"20260806","Name":"MaraCrossing","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6582779125","FullDateString":"6 Aug 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Where two great deserts meet, Joshua Tree National Park reveals a stark, mesmerising landscape shaped by wind, time and extremes. In Southern California, the higher Mojave Desert merges with the hotter, lower Colorado Desert, creating a unique blend of ecosystems and remarkable biodiversity.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SandPath_ROW8239489384_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SandPath_ROW8239489384_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Joshua Tree National Park, California, United States","Copyright":"© JJ Landscapes/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260819_SandPath\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Joshua+Tree+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260819_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260819_SandPath"},"Ssd":"20260819","Name":"SandPath","Market":"ROW","Hash":"8239489384","FullDateString":"19 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Roads have made travel faster for people but created new challenges for wildlife. Highways often cut across their regular migration routes, increasing collisions, fragmenting habitats and isolating animal populations. Wildlife crossings, also known as ecoducts, were developed to reconnect these landscapes. They include vegetated bridges over roads and tunnels beneath them, allowing animals to cross safely while reducing the risk of vehicle collisions. Some of the earliest modern examples appeared in France during the 1950s, while the Netherlands later expanded the idea with wide, green bridges designed to blend into the surrounding landscape.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.WildlifeCrossingPoland_ROW8094277128_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.WildlifeCrossingPoland_ROW8094277128_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Aerial view of a wildlife crossing near Zakrzów, Poland","Copyright":"© bbsferrari/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260818_WildlifeCrossingPoland\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Wildlife+crossing&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260818_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260818_WildlifeCrossingPoland"},"Ssd":"20260818","Name":"WildlifeCrossingPoland","Market":"ROW","Hash":"8094277128","FullDateString":"18 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Location matters. Just ask the false clownfish seen in the image at Lighthouse Reef, near Cabilao Island, Philippines. In these tropical waters packed with hungry mouths and fierce competition, they've secured prime real estate: a sea anemone armed with thousands of microscopic stinging cells.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.CabilaoClowns_ROW7942921985_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.CabilaoClowns_ROW7942921985_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Three false clownfish in a sea anemone, Cabilao Island, Bohol, Philippines","Copyright":"© Franco Banfi/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260817_CabilaoClowns\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=False+clownfish&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260817_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260817_CabilaoClowns"},"Ssd":"20260817","Name":"CabilaoClowns","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7942921985","FullDateString":"17 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Some landscapes are shaped not by people, but by the steady forces of nature over thousands of years. That's exactly the story of Pedra Furada in Jericoacoara, in the Brazilian state of Ceará. Wind and sea gradually carved this natural arch, which has become one of the region's most recognisable landmarks. Located within Jericoacoara National Park, the arch stands along the coast and frames the Atlantic Ocean. From July into early August, visitors gather to watch its most famous spectacle, when the setting sun aligns with the opening in the rock, shining through it for a few minutes before dipping below the horizon.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Furada_ROW7736094795_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Furada_ROW7736094795_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Pedra Furada, Jericoacoara, Brazil","Copyright":"© Brendan van Son/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260816_Furada\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Pedra+Furada+Brazil&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260816_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260816_Furada"},"Ssd":"20260816","Name":"Furada","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7736094795","FullDateString":"16 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"At first glance, it's just a bridge. Then the reflection changes everything. Infinity Bridge spans the River Tees in Stockton-on-Tees, England, where its two striking steel arches and their reflections create the shape of an infinity symbol, inspiring its name. Opened in 2009, the pedestrian and cycle bridge was designed by Expedition Engineering with architect Spence Associates as part of the regeneration of the town's riverside. Stretching 240 metres, its tied-arch structure combines engineering efficiency with a distinctive visual identity.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.StocktonInfinity_ROW7557207458_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.StocktonInfinity_ROW7557207458_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Infinity Bridge in Stockton-on-Tees, England","Copyright":"© Bahadir Yeniceri/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260815_StocktonInfinity\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Infinity+Bridge+England&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260815_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260815_StocktonInfinity"},"Ssd":"20260815","Name":"StocktonInfinity","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7557207458","FullDateString":"15 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"From above, Palmanova looks less like a town and more like a carefully drawn star set into the plains of Friuli-Venezia Giulia, Italy. Founded by the Republic of Venice in 1593, this fortress city was designed for defence, order and spectacle. Its streets radiate from a central square, while its walls are shaped into a precise nine-pointed pattern. That geometry was no accident. Palmanova became one of the most influential models of early modern military architecture. It was protected by concentric fortifications built first under Venice and later strengthened and expanded during the Napoleonic period.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Palmanova_ROW7371050659_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Palmanova_ROW7371050659_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Aerial view of Palmanova, a fortress city in Friuli, Italy","Copyright":"© Riccardo Saponi/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260814_Palmanova\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Palmanova+Italy&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260814_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260814_Palmanova"},"Ssd":"20260814","Name":"Palmanova","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7371050659","FullDateString":"14 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"When darkness falls over Tenerife, Spain, the stars take centre stage. Perched high on the slopes of Mount Teide, Teide Observatory is one of the world's leading solar observatories and among the best places in Europe for astronomical research. Opened in 1964 at an altitude of about 2,390 metres, it benefits from clear skies, dry air and minimal light pollution for much of the year, making it ideal for observing the sun by day and the night sky after sunset.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PerseidasTenerife_ROW7214052413_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PerseidasTenerife_ROW7214052413_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Perseid meteors over Teide Observatory, Tenerife, Spain","Copyright":"© Westend61/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260813_PerseidasTenerife\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Teide+Observatory&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260813_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260813_PerseidasTenerife"},"Ssd":"20260813","Name":"PerseidasTenerife","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7214052413","FullDateString":"13 Aug 2026"}],"LocStrings":{"LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD":"Gambar hari ini","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD_LEARN_MORE":"Pelajari selengkapnya","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_DONATE_NOW":"Berikan donasi sekarang","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_FACT":"Fakta cepat:","LOC_HOMEPAGE_GALLERY_CARD_TITLE":"Gambar Beranda Terbaru","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_GALLERY_IMAGE_ARIALABEL":"Gambar beranda untuk {0}","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ON_THIS_DAY_TITLE":"Hari ini dalam sejarah","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ON_THIS_DAY_IMAGE_ARIALABEL":"Pada hari ini di {0}, {1}","LOC_HOMEPAGE_SHARE_TOOLTIP":"Bagikan beranda Bing hari ini","LOC_HOMEPAGE_WALLPAPERDOWNLOAD_TOOLTIP":"Unduh gambar ini. Penggunaan gambar ini terbatas hanya untuk wallpaper.","LOC_MUSCARD_DOWNLOAD_LINK":"Unduh gambar ini","LOC_HOMEPAGE_WALLPAPERNOTAVAILABLE":"Gambar ini tidak tersedia untuk diunduh sebagai wallpaper.","LOC_HOMEPAGE_INFO_TEXT":"Info","LOC_BING_WP_APP_LINK":"https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2127455","LOC_BING_WP_APP_LINK_TEXT":"Dapatkan aplikasi Bing Wallpaper","LOC_BING_APP_TEXT":"Dapatkan Wallpaper Bing di perangkat Anda","LOC_BING_APP_LINK_PC":"https://bing.microsoftapp.net/bing/?adjust=nk9xri2_dzfz5n2","LOC_BING_APP_LINK_MOBILE":"https://app.adjust.com/d93ddtl_a75k0gg?deeplink=sapphire%